-- A rule that may refuse through a definition two imports away: it calls
-- one that franchise.l4 defines by calling one that franchise.l4 imports
-- from residency.l4. See boolean-rules.l4 for what an "agreement:" line
-- says, and for `pad`.
--
-- agreement: votes may refuse with ["non-residents are not modelled"]
-- agreement: votes {"adult": true, "resident": true} => answers true
-- agreement: votes {"adult": true, "resident": false} => refuses "non-residents are not modelled"
-- agreement: votes {"adult": false, "resident": true} => answers false
-- agreement: votes {"adult": false, "resident": false} => answers false

IMPORT franchise

@export whether the person votes
GIVEN adult IS A BOOLEAN
      resident IS A BOOLEAN
      pad IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE votes IF adult AND `the person may vote` resident
